[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":324},["ShallowReactive",2],{"content-query-ZhH8LW6E7k":3},{"_path":4,"_dir":5,"_draft":6,"_partial":6,"_locale":7,"title":8,"description":9,"date":10,"tags":11,"excerpt":14,"body":24,"_type":318,"_id":319,"_source":320,"_file":321,"_stem":322,"_extension":323},"/blog/vsvode-mouse-lost","blog",false,"","Can't See the Mouse Cursor in VSCode? Here's the Fix!","Recently, I encountered a frustrating issue while using VSCode: the mouse cursor became almost invisible on a light background, especially when switching between the terminal and the editor. This problem was particularly noticeable on Windows systems with AMD graphics cards.","2025-02-04 10:55",[12,13],"vscode","tool",{"type":15,"children":16},"root",[17],{"type":18,"tag":19,"props":20,"children":21},"element","p",{},[22],{"type":23,"value":9},"text",{"type":15,"children":25,"toc":307},[26,30,46,53,69,187,200,261,267,296,301],{"type":18,"tag":19,"props":27,"children":28},{},[29],{"type":23,"value":9},{"type":18,"tag":19,"props":31,"children":32},{},[33,35,44],{"type":23,"value":34},"After some searching, I finally found a solution. By referring to the ",{"type":18,"tag":36,"props":37,"children":41},"a",{"href":38,"rel":39},"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/204181",[40],"nofollow",[42],{"type":23,"value":43},"VSCode GitHub Issue",{"type":23,"value":45},", I discovered that this issue is caused by the Chromium-based rendering mechanism of VSCode. In certain cases, the hardware acceleration or direct composition rendering of VSCode can cause the mouse cursor color to behave abnormally, especially on light backgrounds.",{"type":18,"tag":47,"props":48,"children":50},"h2",{"id":49},"solution",[51],{"type":23,"value":52},"Solution",{"type":18,"tag":54,"props":55,"children":57},"h3",{"id":56},"method-1-disable-hardware-acceleration-disable-hardware-acceleration",[58,60,67],{"type":23,"value":59},"Method 1: Disable Hardware Acceleration (",{"type":18,"tag":61,"props":62,"children":64},